Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">When an ephemeral entity materializes, how does it interact with Arcana? Is a ghost still affected with death or can life or forces affect it as long as it is solid? Ditto with spirit etc.</div> </div> </div> </div>Yes. A materialized ghost is still a ghost, so it is still affected by the Death Arcanum the same way a ghost in Twilight is. Same for sprits, angels, goetia, etc. Although goetia don't typically materialize without help from the Mind Arcanum.<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Newes</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/mage-the-awakening/1047263-materialized-ghosts-spirits-etc#post1047263\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">If a ghost or spirit has or takes on the form of an owl (for example) and then materializes, how obvious would it be that it is not a real owl (assuming the Mortal Mask numina is not involved)? Assuming visually it looks exactly link an owl. Would any perceptual use of life (or death for ghosts or spirit etc.) identify it for what it is?</div> </div> </div> </div>Well, Materialize doesn't change an ephemeral entity's appearance, it just makes it solid and visible to material entities. So a ghost or a spirit of anything but owls can't take on owl form without some kind of Numina that allows it to change form, and even animal spirits tend to look different than the real thing in various ways. Usually the imitation of animals is done by Possessing or at least Urging an animal host with the appropriate resonance. But, assuming that a spirit did for some reason look identical to a normal owl in its natural form? I would say it wouldn't be immediately obvious without magic that it isn't a real owl, but pretty much any supernatural perception involving Life or Spirit would give it away. Or even peripheral Mage Sight if you happen to catch it using a numina or influence. <br /> <br /> &quot;Why is that owl doing magic?&quot;<br /> &quot;Probably a spirit or something.&quot;<br /> &quot;Yeah, that makes sense.&quot;","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Going by Willow now, or Wil for short. She/Her/Hers.","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/269-charlaquin","name":"Charlaquin","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar269_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"10831"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-02-11T11:28:32-08:00","id":1047329,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Charlaquin</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/mage-the-awakening/1047263-materialized-ghosts-spirits-etc?p=1047306#post1047306\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Yes. A materialized ghost is still a ghost, so it is still affected by the Death Arcanum the same way a ghost in Twilight is. Same for sprits, angels, goetia, etc. Although goetia don't typically materialize without help from the Mind Arcanum.<br /> <br /></div> </div> </div> </div>Thanks.<br /> So I follow that it is somehow solidified ephemera, so life or matter wouldn't affect it. But it IS a solid object, so how does a fireball or kinetic blast affect it? Will it damage corpus, or can they only be directly affected by Death / Spirit even for the purpose of damage?<br /> <br /> Also, I know Goetia are mainly the focus of Mind, but it was my understanding that for them to materialize required Death or Spirit magic.<br /> <br />","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/532-newes","name":"Newes","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar532_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"194"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-02-11T11:40:46-08:00","id":1047337,"title":"","content":"Fireballs or kinetic blasts would damage its corpus, which is made up of its ephemera. They would be reduced to Bashing, however, unless they used a bane.<br /> <br /> They need Spirit or Death to gain Manifestations beyond Twilight Form, because they're not from a place that normally has crossover with the real world and don't really come with them.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/886-nofather","name":"nofather","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar886_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"11016"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-02-11T12:00:32-08:00","id":1047342,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Newes</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/mage-the-awakening/1047263-materialized-ghosts-spirits-etc?p=1047329#post1047329\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> Thanks.<br /> So I follow that it is somehow solidified ephemera, so life or matter wouldn't affect it. But it IS a solid object, so how does a fireball or kinetic blast affect it? Will it damage corpus, or can they only be directly affected by Death / Spirit even for the purpose of damage?</div> </div> </div> </div>Physical attacks can affect materialized ephemera, but because their corpus doesn't have vital organs or other vulnerable points, they only take bashing damage from most non-bane sources.<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Newes</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/mage-the-awakening/1047263-materialized-ghosts-spirits-etc?p=1047329#post1047329\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Also, I know Goetia are mainly the focus of Mind, but it was my understanding that for them to materialize required Death or Spirit magic.</div> </div> </div> </div>You're correct, I misremembered the quote. Death or Spirit is required to give them Materialize, Mind is used to give them Possess.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Going by Willow now, or Wil for short. She/Her/Hers.","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/269-charlaquin","name":"Charlaquin","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar269_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"10831"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-02-11T12:11:53-08:00","id":1047343,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Charlaquin</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/mage-the-awakening/1047263-materialized-ghosts-spirits-etc?p=1047342#post1047342\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Physical attacks can affect materialized ephemera, but because their corpus doesn't have vital organs or other vulnerable points, they only take bashing damage from most non-bane sources.<br /> <br /> <br /> You're correct, I misremembered the quote. Death or Spirit is required to give them Materialize, Mind is used to give them Possess.</div> </div> </div> </div>Thank you.<br /> (but I preferred your old avatar)<br /> <br />","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/532-newes","name":"Newes","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar532_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"194"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-02-11T13:19:45-08:00","id":1047371,"title":"","content":"<a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/269-charlaquin\" style=\"background-image:url('https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5//avatar269_2.jpeg');\" class=\"b-bbcode-user b-bbcode-user--has-avatar js-bbcode-user\" data-userid=\"269\" data-vbnamecard=\"269\">Charlaquin</a> Mind 4 can also grant the Familiar Manifestation.